From: UMP <ump@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 87/90] Big packs: leave out the largest content mods instead
 of all, and widen sprite arrays

Past MAX_STATES (2^20 block states) every content mod was refused together: a 300-mod pack (1.14M states) had none of its blocks, with a log line only. fit_states now counts each mod's states without building and leaves out the biggest until the rest fit; each one left out is logged and told to players as they join (with the other left-out mods). Then the pack's 18,134 block textures needed more than eight arrays of 2048 and the game refused to start ('No graphics driver'): layer_split widens the arrays up to the GPU's layer limit when needed (8192 on Vulkan/OpenGL).

UMP top300: 348 content mods load, Diagonal Walls (257,024 states) left out with a chat line; the game starts and plays. Tests: leaves_out_the_biggest_mods_until_the_rest_fit, sprite_split_follows_the_adapters_layer_limit.
